Z||000000||Brian84SE||02-27-2000||07:46 AM||||When does GM official change it's model year.  Mine was manufactured in 8/84 and it's still called an 84. Don't they changeover in July?||||reg||1
Z||000001||Cooter||02-27-2000||11:14 AM||||I believe you missed out on being an 85 by one month!||||reg||1
Z||000002||Monkeyman||02-27-2000||02:04 PM||||They retool in July.  They don't actually start producing the next model year car until late August and it usually doesn't hit the show room until September.  They seem to be changing things, though.  I think it's getting earlier every year.||||reg||1
Z||000003||terryk||02-27-2000||02:41 PM||||July/August. However, they will do rolling changes in many cases meaning they will introduce one change at a time over the 2-3 month period until the new model year is being built. <P>For example, my 86 Ciera 2 door has the slanted rear window. This is actually an 87 feature. The new body style was the first of the production line roll for the 87 cars. It still has many 86 parts.<P>So it's easy to wind up with a car that has both model year features. That's why the parts houses will ask for the VIN or month when you buy parts. On the Ciera, I get asked the chassis code or they ask "slant or square rear window". ||||reg||1
